WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.980
A young man traveled across the ocean to study music.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:11.560
In a far off country, he met a very small and extraordinary creature.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.640
The tiny creature was injured, so feeling pity for it, he treated it.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.700
Upon doing so...

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.410
I owe you my life.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.110
For this, I will grant the blessing of music to the school you build.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.270
Now, some time has passed.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.100
Another extraordinary encounter has taken place.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.390
Who was that guy?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.870
Good luck tomorrow.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.090
Oh, no! I have to hurry!

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.100
Barefoot Vibrato

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.150
Seiso Academy School-wide Music Competition

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:01.990
I made it.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.430
Hey, Hino-san. Good morning.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.410
Good morn...ing.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.650
A-A white tuxedo?!

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.170
Yunoki-sempai, that outfit...

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.290
Does it not suit me?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:19.090
No, it suits you very well, really.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.310
Thank you.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.900
The girls' dressing room is over there.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.010
Good morning, Sempai.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.880
The outfits for the girls really are magnificent.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.970
Thank you so much.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.230
Wh-What's that all about?

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.870
How you doing, Kahoko Hino?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.330
Today's the day, huh?

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.130
Lili!

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.370
What?

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.240
Why is everyone dressed like that?

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:52.240
Why? It's the competition, duh.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.410
Nobody told me that! What should I do?!

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.390
Try this on for size!

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.550
What's this? I don't want this!

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.520
Then how about this?!

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.730
M-My chest...

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.860
M-My legs...

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.230
Hey now.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.580
Don't you have anything more... normal?!

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.240
I already gave you so many options...

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.650
Oh no! I'm late!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.050
Oh, I was just seeing things.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.610
Hihara, that's the girls' dressing room.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.840
I-I-I-I-I'm so sorry, Hino-chan!

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:46.060
Ah, I'm glad it was just Hihara-sempai.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:52.710
I guess this is normal enough.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.680
Good morning, Shimizu-kun.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.150
Good morning.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.040
Wow! You look so sophisticated!

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.670
Did you pick them out yourself?

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.750
No, my older sister sent them to me.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.880
Oh, you have an older sister, Shimizu-kun.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.310
And a younger brother. And a younger sister.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.250
R-Really now?

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.670
Seiso Academy School-wide Music Competition

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.750
I wonder if Kaho will be all right?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:37.180
I'm getting super nervous myself!

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.770
Yunoki-sama...

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.790
That's everyone, right?

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:47.820
Well, today is the first of four selections.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.780
This may sound harsh, but even if you finish last today,

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.860
you still have a chance of winning.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.480
Anyway, enjoy yourselves.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.080
Kanayan! Say something more inspiring!

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.000
I think I'm getting nervous.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.000
You aren't getting nervous, Tsukimori-kun?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.580
Learning to control that is a skill in and of itself.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.920
I see. Everyone gets nervous, huh?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.020
All right, I will announce the performance order.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.600
First up is Shimizu.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.360
Then Hihara.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:18.840
Fuyuumi.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.230
Yunoki.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.690
Hino.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.400
And then Tsukimori.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.860
Well, I wish you all well.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.770
I'm counting on you today.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:32.530
You can count on me, Yunoki-sama.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.840
It'll be fine, Shoko-chan.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.330
Y-Yeah.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.410
I wonder where Shoji-san is.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.500
What's wrong, Hino-chan?

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.170
Oh, Hihara-sempai.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.580
Something on your mind?

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:48.560
Actually, my accompanist isn't here...

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.000
What?! That's-

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.760
The Seiso Academy School-wide Music Competition is beginning.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:05.270
Performer 1, from the Music Department, class 1-A, Keiichi Shimizu-kun.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:09.990
Performing a Boccherini composition, "Cello Concerto in B Flat Major".

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.740
Ah! It's beginning!

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:17.080
Umm, your accompanist is Shoji-san, right?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.420
I'm sure I saw her at school today.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.730
What? Really?

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:21.750
Yes.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.640
Then why...

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.360
He's really putting his heart into it.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.200
The pitch is flawless.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.160
It's a textbook performance.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.710
Incredible...

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:51.620
A first-year can play like that?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.370
Wow, Shimizu-kun is amazing.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:08.460
I'm going to go look for her.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.430
Hino-chan!

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:14.460
Sorry!

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.470
Hino-san! Please don't run in here.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.330
Tsukimori-kun, I'm sorry.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.480
If I'm not back by the time my turn comes up, play ahead of me.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.130
Hey!

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.680
Why?

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:31.860
Performer 2, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Kazuki Hihara-kun.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:37.280
Performing a J.F. Wagner composition, "Unter dem Doppeladler".

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.540
I think I know this piece.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.720
What a fun-sounding song!

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.180
Hino-sempai and Shoji-san aren't back yet, huh?

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:19.960
Ow...

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.660
A blister?

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.400
It's started already?

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.660
Yes.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.240
OK.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.220
I know.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.980
Shoji-

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.990
I never planned on going on stage with her from the start.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:33.670
Huh?

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:37.340
I've prepared a solid alibi. It'll be fine.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.310
What're you doing, Hihara?

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:58.500
I was just so happy, I...

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.170
Don't "happy" me!

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:01.900
Your manners are important, too!

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.970
F-Forget that, Kanayan. Is Hino-chan back yet?

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.540
Hino?

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.140
Come to think of it, Tsukimori is missing, too.

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.480
What's the meaning of this?

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.870
Wait... Are you in that Guard, too?

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:18.980
You know... The Sempai whose name starts with "Yu"...

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.660
Yu

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.610
No. I just don't want you to participate.

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:24.400
Huh?

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:46.220
Performer 3, from the Music Department, class 1-B, Shoko Fuyuumi-san.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.030
Performing a Reger composition, "Romance in G Major".

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:53.660
If you don't have an accompanist, you'll have to withdraw, right?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:57.930
You don't understand the seriousness of music.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.910
Playing Chopin on the violin,

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:04.080
and not putting in enough practice time...

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.450
And you're not only an amateur, but in General Studies...

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:07.520
It's not fair!

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:12.850
Us in the Music Department study music every single day...

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.830
We practice our hearts out!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.200
We're very serious about it!

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.980
You call that being serious?

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.310
Tsukimori-kun...

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:43.210
She's talented, but she seems rather stiff.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:45.190
She must be quite nervous.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:50.770
This is how you choose to use your music that you are so serious about?

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:55.360
Sabotaging the competition in this fashion is an affront

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.690
to all the participants who are serious about their music.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.830
It's a matter of your attitude towards music.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.200
Are you truly serious?

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:11.880
Could it be that she has a crush on Tsukimori-kun?

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.130
Shoji-san!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.520
Shoji-san...

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.300
Ah! I've been looking all over for you!

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:23.880
Hurry back! It's almost your turn!

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.790
I'm sorry. I overstepped my boundaries.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:28.810
It's OK.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:33.280
I knew there were people who don't me well,

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.780
but...

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.270
It hurts.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:43.280
Performer 4, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Azuma Yunoki-kun.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.070
Performing a Grieg composition, "Morning".

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.690
It feels like the start of a pleasant morn.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:08.480
It fits the theme well.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:10.750
His music has a sort of grace to it.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.820
Kanayan! I brought them back!

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:30.120
Pipe down! It's in the middle of a performance.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:34.020
Sheesh. What the heck were you two doing?

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:36.320
Hino, you're up next.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.990
What? Your accompanist isn't here?

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.180
What's the meaning of this?

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:53.930
Well, she suddenly didn't feel well, and...

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:56.860
Where are we going to find a replacement now?

00:13:56.860 --> 00:14:01.350
If you don't have an accompanist, you'll have to withdraw, right?

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.680
Is there anyone here who can accompany her?

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:05.320
That's...

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.500
Hino-san, it's your turn.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.900
I wonder what's going on with Kaho.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:26.330
You don't understand the seriousness of music.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.670
You call that being serious?

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:36.860
It's an affront to all the participants who are serious about their music.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.840
He's right. Everyone is taking this very seriously.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.350
I can't be the only one who doesn't.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:50.020
No matter the circumstances, I was the one who made the final decision to participate.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.540
I can't run away now.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:09.800
Hino!

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:21.730
Performer 5, from General Studies, class 2-2, Kahoko Hino-san.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.370
Kaho-chan!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.300
Why isn't there an accompanist?

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.390
Hey! She's barefoot!

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.360
Hino...

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.410
Performing a Chopin composition, "Tristesse".

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:35.420
Chopin on the violin?

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:39.020
Also, the theme is "A Beginning," but "Tristesse"?

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:41.580
Guess the General Studies students just don't get it.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.400
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:46.480
I'm looking forward to what sort of performance she'll give us.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.090
Do your best, Hino-san.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.550
I don't care about my level.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:57.640
I'm going to give the best performance I can, without overstretching myself.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.120
Are you sure we shouldn't stop her?

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:03.180
Kahoko Hino...

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:08.450
I'll put my genuine self out there for all to see via my violin.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:16.580
Is the violin responding to me,

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.780
or am I responding to the violin?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.940
I just don't want you to participate.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.860
Stop the performance.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:42.390
What happened to your accompanist?

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.520
I don't appreciate you breaking protocol.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.610
Step down at once.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:49.400
Hold on! Maybe we can...

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.040
Doesn't this piece require an accompanist on the piano?

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:52.610
What?

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.570
Well, that's true...

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.200
What should I do?

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:58.700
If she needs accompaniment, then I'll oblige.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.540
What?

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.680
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:24.640
What're you just standing there for?

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:29.070
Let's overlook the little mistakes.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.020
OK!

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.170
Tsuchiura on the piano?

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.380
What the heck is going on?

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:36.360
Hey, you're not a registered student-

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:37.790
Relax, relax.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:43.870
What matters is what and how you express a story through your song.

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.420
"Tristesse."

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.010
What I want to express in this song is...

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:09.010
If you don't burn bridges, then the roads will always open for you.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:12.250
So, this isn't a song of farewell.

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:17.450
It's a song of new beginnings!

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:59.570
It didn't feel forced at all. A truly honest performance.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:02.080
It wasn't tragic, but rather, brilliant.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:06.330
That was great, Hino-chan!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.030
I got really worried there for a minute, but...

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:10.040
Hino-chan!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.130
Hey!

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:15.310
I'm so glad it's over...

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.660
Uh, umm...

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:21.160
Your performance was wonderful.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.130
Thank you.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:26.550
Nice one, Fuyuumi-chan.

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.150
This one would be no good, huh?

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:30.630
Ah! Don't let anyone see that, Yunoki!

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:31.750
Damn you!

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:33.860
Sorry, but can you let me through?

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:36.170
I'm sorry!

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:47.290
Performer 6, from the Music Department, class 2-A, Len Tsukimori-kun.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:51.910
Performing a Wieniawski composition, "Polonaise Brillante No. 1".

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.560
The audience is still buzzing.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.830
Maybe the performance had some effect on them.

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:33.680
It's so lovely and powerful...

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.430
It's almost overwhelming.

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:37.870
It's perfect... isn't it?

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:44.160
It's powerful... Like he's blazing a trail somewhere.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.060
It's the embodiment of "A Beginning".

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:58.510
And then, Tsukimori-kun closed the first selection and took first place.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:38.000
I realize now that I did something rather shameless out here.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:39.580
But...

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:46.480
What I felt out here, I can't put into words.

00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:47.270
Hino?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:48.270
Huh?

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:49.980
You haven't gone home yet?

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:51.390
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:55.830
I'm sorry you finished last even after you went through the trouble of accompanying me.

00:22:55.830 --> 00:22:58.150
What're you talking about?

00:22:58.150 --> 00:23:00.730
I never expected you to play "Tristesse".

00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:03.190
You like that song, huh?

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.350
You got me there.

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:08.680
You gave a pretty good performance.

00:23:08.680 --> 00:23:10.370
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:13.880
Thanks so much for everything.

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:17.460
It was thanks to you that I was able to give it my all.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:19.850
Really, it was nothing.

00:23:20.810 --> 00:23:23.030
Anyway, I'm taking off.

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:34.360
That really was some performance.

00:23:36.840 --> 00:23:40.240
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.230
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:48.550
Chopin was born in Poland and became a famous composer and pianist in Paris in the 19th century.

00:23:48.550 --> 00:23:54.010
He composed multiple masterpieces including "24 Preludes" and "Heroic Polonaise".

00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:56.930
He's even been referred to as the "Poet of the Piano".

00:23:57.450 --> 00:23:59.380
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:03.040
Which country does polonaise music originate from?

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.610
The answer is at the end of this program!

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:10.380
Next Episode

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:07.930
What? Three nights and four days?

00:24:07.930 --> 00:24:10.380
Just us inside this amazing villa?

